Request Time: 1 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":1700,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"c0aa6076e0834b3f2ec32904804fb186","RawContent":"&lt;div style=\"margin:20px; margin-top:5px; \"&gt; &lt;div class=\"smallfont\"&gt;Quote:&lt;\/div&gt; &lt;table cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"99%\"&gt; &lt;tr&gt; &lt;td class=\"alt2\" style=\"border:1px inset\"&gt;  Originally Posted by &lt;strong&gt;carlymcmullen&lt;\/strong&gt; &lt;img class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"View Post\"&gt;  &lt;div style=\"font-style:italic\"&gt;Thanks, Julie! I love seeing &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; people in the dresses. I had seen this dress on teh model in a magazine and on the website and I didn&#039;t even take another glance at it. In person it was just gorgeous. I made my final payment and just waiting for the check to clear and I can pick it up! I am afraid that when I pick it up, I will need to try it on every morning, every night when i get home from work and then again before I go to bed. That is, if I can take it off at all! Hhahahahaaa.&lt;\/div&gt; &lt;\/td&gt; &lt;\/tr&gt; &lt;\/table&gt; &lt;\/div&gt;I thought I would be the same way, but I didn&#039;t try it on at all. I took it in for alterations a few days after I got it, and she kept it there for me till I came back for a fitting and she had it till about a week before the wedding, I had my final fitting then took it to the store to be steamed and picked it up the day before we left. That was the best way for me. No chance DH would see it and no chance I would try it on and rip it or spill something on it, both nightmares of mine.","Attachments":[],"Id":139836,"PostDate":1195228912,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <div  style=\"margin:20px\"> <div class=\"smallfont\">Quote:<\/div> <table cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"99%\"> <tr> <td class=\"alt2\" style=\"border:1px inset\">  Originally Posted by <strong>carlymcmullen<\/strong> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"View Post\"><\/span>  <div  style=\"font-style:italic\">Thanks, Julie! I love seeing \"real\" people in the dresses. I had seen this dress on teh model in a magazine and on the website and I didn't even take another glance at it. In person it was just gorgeous. I made my final payment and just waiting for the check to clear and I can pick it up! I am afraid that when I pick it up, I will need to try it on every morning, every night when i get home from work and then again before I go to bed. That is, if I can take it off at all! Hhahahahaaa.<\/div> <\/td> <\/tr> <\/table> <\/div>I thought I would be the same way, but I didn't try it on at all. I took it in for alterations a few days after I got it, and she kept it there for me till I came back for a fitting and she had it till about a week before the wedding, I had my final fitting then took it to the store to be steamed and picked it up the day before we left. That was the best way for me. No chance DH would see it and no chance I would try it on and rip it or spill something on it, both nightmares of mine.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"graberjul@gmail.com","IpAddress":"173.33.230.91","GroupId":46,"GroupNa